author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Preserve explicit completed-at and immutable closure evidence; expose whether completed_at was supplied or inferred; document retroactive closure behavior across SDK/CLI/MCP.
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "SDK close distinguishes asserted, existing and inferred completion timestamps, seals timestamp/source under the item lock, preserves compact and bulk receipts, and supplies correction guidance. Bulk normalization preserves explicit canonical/snake-case timestamps. Portable history and existing JSON key prefixes are retained; token replays consume the added context with narrowly documented ceilings."
expected_result: "Retroactive closes expose inference, explicit and existing dates survive every transport, and immutable history remains reproducible and independently verifiable."
actual_result: "87 focused tests and both linked owners pass, including negative-before provenance controls, independent-process reproducibility, exact attribution and output ordering. Packed npm/npx/Bun/bunx and nine-package smoke pass. Strengthened token replay and seeded-growth rejection pass. Final static and hosted full coverage remain merge requirements."
