  "2026-10-25T14:04:42.306Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: pair completion-time provenance with pm-gh1585 refusal-side-effect disclosure in one SDK-first PR. Complete strict all-status baseline: 3109 items, 2821 closed, 215 open, 59 draft, 14 canceled, zero in_progress, zero omissions/unreadable records. Preserve asserted dates, prior completion values, and immutable close evidence; add actionable transport receipts and independent regression controls."
  "2026-10-25T14:10:37.814Z","harness:codex","Sandbox reproduction: new close-provenance controls fail on baseline because completion receipts/history context are absent. While extending bulk acceptance, found closeManyOptionsFromFlat drops completedAt despite the documented bulk option; include this related SDK/MCP adapter fix under the same owner. The implementation preserves existing terminal completion values and reports asserted/existing/close_time per close event, with an executable evidence-only update hint for inference."
  "2026-10-25T14:14:00.141Z","harness:codex","GitHub intake audit: all29 open issues have a comment linking canonical PM lineage; no duplicate comments posted. Current mutation-audit work reuses the two existing owners. The latest pm-changelog2026.10.25 package is installed through the configured package-owned pipeline, with no generator implementation changes in pm-cli."
  "2026-10-25T14:34:40.179Z","harness:codex","Full-suite feedback applied: immutable context stores only completion timestamp/source, retaining cross-workspace byte reproducibility; local hints remain response-only. Full close JSON preserves item/changed_fields/warnings order and appends completion. Exact harness-history assertions retain every provenance field while accepting the new close context. Added canonical/snake-case bulk completion normalization and precedence coverage. Original full run retained11366 passing/4 failing tests; three related failures are now covered by the revised focused run, and the independent npm module-discovery environment issue remains under pm-bj7rq0."
  "2026-10-25T14:37:41.524Z","harness:codex","Revised acceptance passes87 tests across seven files, including the previously failing reproducibility, deterministic output and harness attribution controls. Both linked owner test runs now pass with the already built checkout and no build-lease contention. Canonical/snake-case bulk completion values retain precedence; no history rewriter or completion-time guesser was added. Final static, packed-consumer and hosted exact-coverage gates remain required before merge."
  "2026-10-25T14:43:57.049Z","harness:codex","Packed acceptance passes for the current checkout: npm/npx and Bun/bunx smoke, with all nine bundled packages. Independent npm registry timestamps confirm eight latest candidates remain younger than the seven-day adoption boundary; the eligible major migrations retain existing canonical owners. No open dependency PR or security alert is present. Current PR changes remain restricted to mutation audit contracts, their regression owners, docs, generated surface/changelog and live evidence."
  "2026-10-25T14:46:35.933Z","harness:codex","The unchanged task replay correctly refused new receipt cost: lifecycle close adds76 estimated tokens and partial bulk adds80. Strengthen both existing transcripts to require completion timestamp, source=close_time and correction guidance; regenerate their reviewed baseline with explicit quality-evidence rationale. No task, field, outcome, byte-accounting check or negative control is removed. Verify that only the two relevant task/step ceilings plus their composite change, and rerun the seeded-growth negative control before static admission."
  "2026-10-25T14:48:56.015Z","harness:codex","Token proof: the real replay satisfies the strengthened required-field contracts; retained all unrelated historical ceilings and orientation metadata instead of accepting incidental tighter regeneration. Only lifecycle close(+76), partial bulk(+80), their task ceilings and composite(+156) change. The seeded extra1,000,000-token report is rejected by the original comparison logic. Local tracker validation is ok with the pre-existing historical resolution-field warning population; full history integrity remains required."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T14:11:53.698Z","harness:codex","A completion value and its provenance are separate contracts. Preserve existing metadata without claiming it was asserted, seal provenance in the same locked close event, and keep it visible in compact receipts and bulk rows."
